   1            /
   2            /   Clear Memory
   3            /
   4            *3000
   5            AUTO=DEP-COUNT          / NOTE: Must be the address of an autoindex!
   6 03000 0016 COUNT,  DEP-COUNT+2     / Words to clear
   7 03001 3015 TO,     DEP+1           / 10
   8 03002 3601 LOOP,   DCA I TO        / Erase most of memory
   9 03003 2201         ISZ TO
  10 03004 2200         ISZ COUNT
  11 03005 5202         JMP LOOP
  12 03006 3203         DCA .-3         / Kill the loop.
  13 03007 3204         DCA .-3
  14 03010 3205         DCA .-3
  15                    / At this point, all of memory except this program 
  16                    / has been erased, and TO points at this program.
  17                    / (That also implies it has a value of 3001, a harmless 
  18                    / DCA instruction.)
  19 03011 1201         TAD TO
  20 03012 3014         DCA AUTO        / Set up autoindex register
  21 03013 3212         DCA .-1         / But only once.
  22 03014 3414 DEP,    DCA I AUTO      / Zero a word of this program
  23                    / Now we loop through all of core, clearing a single 
  24                    / word on each pass, until we clear DEP.
  25                    / We have arranged that DEP lives at an address that 
  26                    / doubles as a DCA AUTO instruction.  That instruction
  27                    / is now in location AUTO.  Fall through memory one 
  28                    / more time, until we hit it.
  29            /
  30            / Load Cruft before and after, to test boundary cases.
  31 03015 7402         HLT
  32            *2777
  33 02777 7402         HLT
  34            
  35            $
